\section{Introduction}
Basque (Euskara, ISO 639-3 eus) is a language isolate, official in the Basque Autonomous Community and parts of Navarre, and used as a language of instruction. The Basque Country and Navarre run bilingual schooling in models A, B and D by degree of Basque-medium teaching, and the northern Basque Country offers immersion and bilingual tracks. This list is limited to what the searches surfaced.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Basque acquisition planning (Basque Government publication, English): \url{https://euskadi.eus/contenidos/informacion/dia6/en_2027/adjuntos/publications_in_english/basque_acquisition_planning_en.pdf}
\item Tokian tokiko hizkuntzak eskolan: Derioko euskara ikasteko proposamena (EHU repository): \url{https://addi.ehu.es/handle/10810/55067}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Elhuyar Hiztegia (Basque-Spanish/Spanish-Basque dictionary, about 92,500 entries), help page: \url{https://www.euskadi.eus/ab34aElhuyarHiztegiaWar/ab34ahiztegia}
\item Elhuyar announcement of the updated dictionary: \url{https://zientzia.eus/artikuluak/elhuyar-hiztegiaren-argitalpen-eguneratua-eta-osat/en/}
\item Free Basque learning books list (aggregator, includes a grammar introduction by Itziar Laka): \url{https://www.infobooks.org/free-pdf-books/language-learning/basque-learning}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
Nothing specific was found in the searches.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Etxepare Basque Institute, Learn Basque: \url{https://www.etxepare.eus/en/learn-basque}
